    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A coefficient in front of a log can move up as a power.\n\n3 log₂4 = log₂(4^3).\nSince 4=2^2, this is 3×2=6.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The power law is:\n\nlog_a(x^p)=p log_a x\n\nYou can move the power down as a multiplier, or move a multiplier up as a power.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
