    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A logarithm and an exponential with the same base undo each other.\n\na^(log_a x)=x.\n\nFor example, 5^(log₅7)=7.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Why? If log_a x=m, then a^m=x by definition. The expression simply puts that exponent back onto the same base.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
